      "id": "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::backward_beta_physics_coupling",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Leaky::backward() uses self.beta for gradient but in Physics mode beta is a derived quantity",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "contract_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/neurons/lif/backward.rs",
          "src/neurons/lif/builder.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "backward.rs line 20: grad_mem_prev = &grad_mem * self.beta. In physics mode, beta = exp(-dt/tau_m) which is set during construction. The backward pass silently depends on beta being correctly synced, but there's no comment explaining this coupling."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Add a doc comment to backward() explaining that self.beta is used as the membrane decay factor for both modes, and that in physics mode it equals exp(-dt/tau_m) as set during construction. Alternatively, compute the decay factor directly from mode parameters.",
