      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::simulation_state_wide_options",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "SimulationState uses Option for fields that are always Some during active simulation",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "src/web/simulation.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "SimulationState has network: Option<Network>, test_images: Option<Array2<f32>>, test_labels: Option<Vec<usize>> that are None only before load_checkpoint is called. During active simulation all three are always Some, but every access must unwrap or check."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Consider splitting into SimulationConfig (idle, no network) and LoadedSimulation (always has network, images, labels) using an enum. Alternatively, document the invariant and use a helper method that returns a struct reference with non-optional fields.",
