      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::partial_cmp_unwrap_nan",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "f32 partial_cmp().unwrap() in spice.rs and inspector.rs will panic on NaN values",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/spice.rs",
          "src/inspector.rs",
          "src/cli/commands/spice.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "spice.rs line 1241: .max_by(|(_, a), (_, b)| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap())",
          "spice.rs line 1248: same pattern",
          "inspector.rs line 146: same pattern",
          "cli/commands/spice.rs line 146: same pattern",
          "If any value in the compared collection is NaN, partial_cmp returns None and unwrap panics"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace .partial_cmp(b).unwrap() with .partial_cmp(b).unwrap_or(std::cmp::Ordering::Equal) or use total_cmp() which is available on f32 since Rust 1.62.",
