    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::mutex_unwrap_no_poisoning": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::mutex_unwrap_no_poisoning",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Animation and dashboard code uses .lock().unwrap() on Mutex without poisoning recovery",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/animation.rs",
          "src/dashboard.rs",
          "src/cli/commands/animate.rs",
          "src/cli/commands/dashboard.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "18 instances of .lock().unwrap() in animation/animate command code, 3 in dashboard -- if any thread panics while holding the lock, all subsequent access panics",
          "These are in UI code where a thread panic (e.g., from a rendering error) could cascade"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace .lock().unwrap() with .lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner()) to recover from poisoned mutexes, or wrap in a helper function that logs the poisoning and recovers. This is a standard pattern for UI code where data corruption is preferable to crashing.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "4630fdbb"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-19T20:47:07+00:00",
